  "method_card": {
   "steps": [
    "Write the proportion as an equation with k, e.g. y = kx²",
    "Substitute the known pair to find k",
    "Put k back in, then substitute the new value",
    "Shortcut: y ∝ x² means ×2 on x gives ×4 on y; y ∝ 1/x² means ÷4"
   ],
   "title": "Proportion with Powers",
   "content": "<p>Proportion can involve powers: \\(y \\propto x^2\\) means \\(y = kx^2\\). Similarly \\(y \\propto \\sqrt{x}\\) means \\(y = k\\sqrt{x}\\), and \\(y \\propto \\frac{1}{x^2}\\) means \\(y = \\frac{k}{x^2}\\).</p>",
   "example": "<p><strong>\\(y \\propto x^2\\). When \\(x = 3\\), \\(y = 36\\). Find \\(y\\) when \\(x = 5\\).</strong></p><p>\\(k = 36/9 = 4\\). \\(y = 4 \\times 25 = 100\\).</p>"
  },
  "tier_guides": {
   "gold": {
    "steps": [
     "Gold mixes cubes \\(y \\propto x^3\\), inverse roots \\(y \\propto \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\), and real formulas (\\(P \\propto \\frac{1}{V}\\), \\(T \\propto \\sqrt{L}\\)).",
     "The method never changes: form the equation, find k from the given pair, then substitute or reverse for the unknown.",
     "Reversing through a power needs the matching root: cube root for x³, square root for x²."
    ],
    "title": "Gold: cube and root laws in context",
    "example": {
     "steps": [
      {
       "label": "Find k",
       "content": "<p>\\(k = 54 ÷ 3^3 = 54 ÷ 27 = 2\\)</p>"
